<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alcuin of York</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Alcuin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alcuin of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a> was an English scholar and teacher who joined the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> in the late eighth century. He led the palace school and played a leading role in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-renaissance">Carolingian Renaissance</a>, promoting education, the copying of texts and reforms of script and liturgy. He later became abbot of St Martin's at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tours">Tours</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alcuin-of-york.jpg" alt="Alcuin of York" width="320" height="341" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fulda · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raban-Maur_Alcuin_Otgar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
